  "identifier": "medical-note-eval",
  "name": "Medical Note-Eval (Note-Eval v2)",
  "alternateName": [
    "Note-Eval v2",
    "Omi medical-note-eval"
  ],
  "description": "Open benchmark and reproducible evaluation framework from Omi Health for the safety of AI-generated clinical notes. It runs 8 frontier writer models over 300 synthetic ambulatory primary-care doctor-patient dialogues and scores the generated SOAP notes for prose quality, hallucinations, and omitted safety-critical information using a 4-verifier cross-family LLM judge panel plus clinician-blind prose scoring. Headline finding: across 2,400 notes, omissions were ~43× more common than fabrications (520 safety-relevant facts dropped vs 12 confirmed high-impact hallucinations). Also evaluates 'Omi Guard', a transcript-grounded safety layer that recovered all 520 omitted facts with zero new hallucinations. The repository publishes all 4,800 before/after notes, token data, and scoring scripts for independent verification. MIT-licensed. Note: the benchmark evaluates several proprietary models (e.g. GPT, Claude, Gemini, DeepSeek), but the benchmark corpus and code themselves are open.",
